description:
Execute a JavaScript snippet inside an isolated QuickJS WASM sandbox with direct synchronous/async access to the Hotyata SDK (`sdk`).
Use this "MCP Code Mode" tool whenever you need to run multi-step queries, compare multiple categories/districts/stages, join complexes with properties, filter or aggregate results, and return only a compact final summary in a single round-trip.

Available global `sdk` methods inside your script (can be called with or without `await`):
- `sdk.searchProperties(params)` -> `{ total, page, limit, properties: [...] }`
- `sdk.getPropertyStats(params)` -> `{ city, deal_type, group_by, total_matching_listings, groups: [...] }`
- `sdk.getProperty(idOrArrayOfIds)` -> property details object or `{ properties: [...] }`
- `sdk.searchComplexes(params)` -> `{ total, page, limit, complexes: [...] }`
- `sdk.getComplex(idOrArrayOfIds)` -> complex details object or `{ complexes: [...] }`
- `sdk.searchItems(params)` -> `{ total, page, limit, items: [...] }`
- `sdk.getItem(idOrArrayOfIds)` -> item details object or `{ items: [...] }`

<examples>
// Example 1: Compare renovation status & off-plan (katlavan) sale dynamics in Batumi
const byRenovation = sdk.getPropertyStats({ city: "batumi", deal_type: "sale", group_by: "renovation_status" });
const byStage = sdk.getPropertyStats({ city: "batumi", deal_type: "sale", group_by: "construction_stage" });
return { byRenovation: byRenovation.groups, byStage: byStage.groups };

// Example 2: Multi-search classifieds and return top 3 cheapest per item type
const queries = ["4K monitor", "router", "electric heater", "mechanical keyboard"];
return queries.map(q => {
  const res = sdk.searchItems({ query: q, sort: "cheapest", limit: 3 });
  return { query: q, total: res.total, cheapest: res.items.map(i => ({ id: i.id, title: i.title, price_gel: i.price_gel, price_usd: i.price_usd, url: i.canonical_url })) };
});
</examples>
<hints>
- Write a function body ending with a `return ...;` statement.
- Maximum 15 SDK calls per execution. Memory limit: 32MB, CPU timeout: 5s.
</hints>
